# Self notes

## Taints and tolerations
- General proccess: Set a "Taint" on nodes, then set "Tolerations" to those "Taints" on the pods.  

### Problem:
- In a cluster of 5 nodes, if 3 are tainted, and 2 others are general purpose.
- There is a chance that a pod, marked with a toleration, will be scheduled to a general purpose node.

## Node Affinity
- In the node def, you define a set of labels. In the pod def, you degine the set of nodes, that it is allowed to be scheduled to.

### Problem:
- In same 5 node cluster scenario. There is a chance that a general purpse node, gets scheduled on a "node affinity" node.

## Resolution to both problems:
- Using a combination of both, T&T with NA. 
- Idea, set a group of nodes under a speficic label and taint. Then, your group of speficfied pods set under a spefic toleration and affinity. 
